IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc25-alternative-measures.l4 -- Part XXII.2 Alternative Measures and Restorative Justice Processes of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: sections 715.44 to 715.6
-- (definitions, purpose and principles, warnings and referrals, conditions for and restrictions on alternative measures, restorative justice processes, conferences, records).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source and result conventions are those stated at the head of ccc25-remediation-negotiation.l4 (JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words;
-- NOTHING where the text does not answer, including a grant named "may" whose "if" gate fails: the coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-12, one fork line per site in NOTES.md).
-- "Police officer" is not a defined term of the Code. The core's Party has `a peace officer` (s 2) and no police officer, so `a peace officer` stands for it (fork F6).

§ `Section 715.44 -- Definitions (Part XXII.2)`

-- 715.44 lead-in "The following definitions apply in this Part." sets the scope of the three definitions below: no rule of its own (coverage row, inert, reason 1).

-- alternative measures means measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act that are applicable in respect of a person who is 18 years of age or older and is alleged to have committed an offence.
-- src:15040 | alternative measures means measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act that are applicable in respect of a person who is 18 years of age or older and is alleged to have committed an offence. (mesures de rechange)
@ref s 715.44 "alternative measures" (src:15040-15040)
GIVEN `the measures are measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the measures are applicable in respect of a person who is alleged to have committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the age of that person in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.44 alternative measures` MEANS
    IF `the measures are measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act` AND `the measures are applicable in respect of a person who is alleged to have committed an offence` AND `the age of that person in years` AT LEAST 18
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "alternative measures means measures other than judicial proceedings under this Act that are applicable in respect of a person who is 18 years of age or older and is alleged to have committed an offence"

-- restorative justice, in respect of the criminal justice system, means an approach to justice that seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships.
-- src:15041 | restorative justice, in respect of the criminal justice system, means an approach to justice that seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships. (justice réparatrice)
@ref s 715.44 "restorative justice" (src:15041-15041)
GIVEN `it is an approach to justice in respect of the criminal justice system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.44 restorative justice` MEANS
    IF `it is an approach to justice in respect of the criminal justice system` AND `it seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "restorative justice, in respect of the criminal justice system, means an approach to justice that seeks to repair the harm caused by an offence to individuals and their relationships"

-- restorative justice process means a process that provides an opportunity for a person alleged to have committed an offence, an offender, a victim or members of a community, as the case may be,
-- to communicate, directly or indirectly, about the causes, circumstances and impacts of an offence or alleged offence in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused.
-- src:15042 | restorative justice process means a process that provides an opportunity for a person alleged to have committed an offence, an offender, a victim or members of a community, as the case may be, to communicate, directly or indirectly, about the causes, circumstances and impacts of an offence or alleged offence in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused. (processus de justice réparatrice)
@ref s 715.44 "restorative justice process" (src:15042-15042)
GIVEN `it is a process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides an opportunity, as the case may be, for a person alleged to have committed an offence, an offender, a victim or members of a community to communicate, directly or indirectly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is about the causes, circumstances and impacts of an offence or alleged offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the communication is in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.44 restorative justice process` MEANS
    IF `it is a process` AND `it provides an opportunity, as the case may be, for a person alleged to have committed an offence, an offender, a victim or members of a community to communicate, directly or indirectly` AND `the communication is about the causes, circumstances and impacts of an offence or alleged offence` AND `the communication is in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "restorative justice process means a process that provides an opportunity ... in order to seek a resolution to repair the harm caused"

§ `Sections 715.45 and 715.46 -- Purpose and principles`

-- 715.45 The purpose of this Part is to contribute to the respect for the law and the maintenance of a just, peaceful and safe society, including by (a) to (e).
-- The clause states a purpose and creates no rule: coverage rows, inert, reason 1. It is kept as quotation so that a reader holding the source beside this module sees nothing skipped.
-- src:15046 | 715.45 The purpose of this Part is to contribute to the respect for the law and the maintenance of a just, peaceful and safe society, including by
-- src:15047 | (a) holding a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender accountable in respect of the offence or alleged offence;
-- src:15048 | (b) promoting a sense of responsibility for the offence or alleged offence and acknowledging the harm caused to the victim and the community;
-- src:15049 | (c) repairing the harm caused to the victim and the community;
-- src:15050 | (d) promoting the rehabilitation and reintegration of the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender; and
-- src:15051 | (e) preventing further harm and involvement in the criminal justice system.
@ref s 715.45 (src:15046-15051)
`s 715.45 the purpose of this Part as the text states it` MEANS "to contribute to the respect for the law and the maintenance of a just, peaceful and safe society"

-- 715.46 The following principles apply to this Part: (a) to (d). A table: each named principle applies; any other statement is not covered (the list is not closed with "only").
-- src:15053 | 715.46 The following principles apply to this Part:
-- src:15054 | (a) judicial resources are more appropriately used in relation to offences that pose a risk to the safety of the public;
-- src:15055 | (b) measures that are taken under this Part allow for effective and timely intervention focused on addressing the circumstances underlying the offence or alleged offence;
-- src:15056 | (c) crime has a harmful impact on victims and on society and measures that are taken under this Part should take into consideration their interests; and
-- src:15057 | (d) measures that are taken under this Part take into account the personal circumstances and characteristics of the person alleged to have committed the offence or of the offender and of the victim, as the case may be, with particular attention to the needs of Aboriginal persons and Black persons.
@ref s 715.46 (src:15053-15057)
DECLARE `s 715.46 the principle` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.46(a) judicial resources are more appropriately used in relation to offences that pose a risk to the safety of the public`
    `s 715.46(b) measures that are taken under this Part allow for effective and timely intervention focused on addressing the circumstances underlying the offence or alleged offence`
    `s 715.46(c) crime has a harmful impact on victims and on society and measures that are taken under this Part should take into consideration their interests`
    `s 715.46(d) measures that are taken under this Part take into account the personal circumstances and characteristics of the person alleged to have committed the offence or of the offender and of the victim, as the case may be, with particular attention to the needs of Aboriginal persons and Black persons`
    `s 715.46 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names`

@ref s 715.46 (src:15053-15057)
GIVEN principle IS A `s 715.46 the principle`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.46 the principle applies to this Part` MEANS
    CONSIDER principle
    WHEN `s 715.46(a) judicial resources are more appropriately used in relation to offences that pose a risk to the safety of the public` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.46(b) measures that are taken under this Part allow for effective and timely intervention focused on addressing the circumstances underlying the offence or alleged offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.46(c) crime has a harmful impact on victims and on society and measures that are taken under this Part should take into consideration their interests` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.46(d) measures that are taken under this Part take into account the personal circumstances and characteristics of the person alleged to have committed the offence or of the offender and of the victim, as the case may be, with particular attention to the needs of Aboriginal persons and Black persons` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.46 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following principles apply to this Part"

§ `Sections 715.47 and 715.48 -- Warnings and referrals by the police and by the prosecutor`

-- 715.47 (1) A police officer must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence
-- and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, instead of proceeding with the laying of an information against the person alleged to have committed the offence,
-- (a) taking no further action; (b) issuing a warning to the person; or (c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure.
-- A duty to consider, with an "if" gate (fork F8: a duty whose "if" is unmet is JUST FALSE). The duty is only to consider; the options are the three listed.
-- src:15061 | 715.47 (1) A police officer must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, instead of proceeding with the laying of an information against the person alleged to have committed the offence,
-- src:15062 | (a) taking no further action;
-- src:15063 | (b) issuing a warning to the person; or
-- src:15064 | (c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure.
@ref s 715.47(1) (src:15061-15064)
DECLARE `s 715.47(1) the option` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.47(1)(a) taking no further action`
    `s 715.47(1)(b) issuing a warning to the person`
    `s 715.47(1)(c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure`
    `s 715.47(1) an option that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names`

@ref s 715.47(1) (src:15061-15064)
GIVEN option IS A `s 715.47(1) the option`
      `it is appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it poses a risk to the safety of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.47(1) the police officer must consider the option instead of proceeding with the laying of an information` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is appropriate in the circumstances`) OR `it poses a risk to the safety of the public`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public"
    ELSE CONSIDER option
         WHEN `s 715.47(1)(a) taking no further action` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.47(1)(b) issuing a warning to the person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.47(1)(c) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or, if authorized to do so, to an alternative measure` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 715.47(1) an option that none of paragraphs (a) to (c) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consider, instead of proceeding with the laying of an information against the person alleged to have committed the offence, (a) taking no further action; (b) issuing a warning to the person; or (c)"

-- 715.47 (2) The failure of a police officer to consider the options set out in subsection (1) does not invalidate any subsequent charges against the person for the offence.
-- src:15066 | (2) The failure of a police officer to consider the options set out in subsection (1) does not invalidate any subsequent charges against the person for the offence.
@ref s 715.47(2) (src:15066-15066)
GIVEN `the police officer failed to consider the options set out in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the charges are subsequent charges against the person for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.47(2) the failure of the police officer to consider the options invalidates the subsequent charges` MEANS
    IF `the police officer failed to consider the options set out in subsection (1)` AND `the charges are subsequent charges against the person for the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not invalidate any subsequent charges against the person for the offence"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The failure of a police officer to consider the options set out in subsection (1)"

-- 715.48 (1) A prosecutor must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence
-- and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence, (a) issuing a warning to the person; or
-- (b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure.
-- src:15068 | 715.48 (1) A prosecutor must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence,
-- src:15069 | (a) issuing a warning to the person; or
-- src:15070 | (b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure.
@ref s 715.48(1) (src:15068-15070)
DECLARE `s 715.48(1) the option` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.48(1)(a) issuing a warning to the person`
    `s 715.48(1)(b) with the consent of the person, referring them to a program or to an agency or another service provider in the community that may assist them or to an alternative measure`
    `s 715.48(1) an option that neither paragraph (a) nor (b) names`

@ref s 715.48(1) (src:15068-15070)
GIVEN option IS A `s 715.48(1) the option`
      `it is before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appropriate in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it poses a risk to the safety of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.48(1) the prosecutor must consider the option before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consider, before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence"
        IF (NOT `it is appropriate in the circumstances`) OR `it poses a risk to the safety of the public` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public"
        IF option EQUALS `s 715.48(1) an option that neither paragraph (a) nor (b) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "consider ... (a) issuing a warning to the person; or (b)"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.48 (2) The failure of a prosecutor to consider the options set out in subsection (1) does not invalidate any proceedings against the person for the offence.
-- src:15072 | (2) The failure of a prosecutor to consider the options set out in subsection (1) does not invalidate any proceedings against the person for the offence.
@ref s 715.48(2) (src:15072-15072)
GIVEN `the prosecutor failed to consider the options set out in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings against the person for the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.48(2) the failure of the prosecutor to consider the options invalidates the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the prosecutor failed to consider the options set out in subsection (1)` AND `the proceedings are proceedings against the person for the offence`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not invalidate any proceedings against the person for the offence"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The failure of a prosecutor to consider the options set out in subsection (1)"

§ `Sections 715.49 to 715.52 -- Alternative measures: conditions, restrictions, effect`

-- 715.49 Alternative measures may be used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met: (a) to (g).
-- A grant ("may") with an "if" gate that the text does not close with "only if": when a condition is not met the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (the coordinator's ruling of 2026-11-12; fork F2).
-- Condition (g), "not in any way barred at law", asks about law outside this range: it is a plain input, never guessed.
-- src:15078 | 715.49 Alternative measures may be used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met:
-- src:15079 | (a) the alternative measures are part of a program of alternative measures authorized by the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s delegate or authorized by a person, or a person within a class of persons, designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province;
-- src:15080 | (b) the person who is considering whether to use the alternative measure is satisfied that it would be appropriate, having regard to the needs of the person alleged to have committed the offence and the interests of the victim and of society;
-- src:15081 | (c) the person alleged to have committed the offence, having been informed of the alternative measure, fully and freely consents to participate in it;
-- src:15082 | (d) the person alleged to have committed the offence has, before consenting to participate in the alternative measure, been advised of the right to be represented by counsel;
-- src:15083 | (e) the person alleged to have committed the offence accepts responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence;
-- src:15084 | (f) in the opinion of the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s agent, there is sufficient evidence to proceed with the prosecution of the offence; and
-- src:15085 | (g) the prosecution of the offence is not in any way barred at law.
@ref s 715.49 (src:15078-15085)
DECLARE `s 715.49 what the facts show` HAS
    `(a) the alternative measures are part of a program of alternative measures authorized by the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s delegate or authorized by a person, or a person within a class of persons, designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(b) the person who is considering whether to use the alternative measure is satisfied that it would be appropriate, having regard to the needs of the person alleged to have committed the offence and the interests of the victim and of society`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(c) the person alleged to have committed the offence, having been informed of the alternative measure, fully and freely consents to participate in it`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(d) the person alleged to have committed the offence has, before consenting to participate in the alternative measure, been advised of the right to be represented by counsel`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(e) the person alleged to have committed the offence accepts responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(f) in the opinion of the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s agent, there is sufficient evidence to proceed with the prosecution of the offence`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `(g) the prosecution of the offence is not in any way barred at law`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 715.49 (src:15078-15085)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 715.49 what the facts show`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.49 alternative measures may be used in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence` MEANS
    IF     facts's `(a) the alternative measures are part of a program of alternative measures authorized by the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s delegate or authorized by a person, or a person within a class of persons, designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province`
       AND facts's `(b) the person who is considering whether to use the alternative measure is satisfied that it would be appropriate, having regard to the needs of the person alleged to have committed the offence and the interests of the victim and of society`
       AND facts's `(c) the person alleged to have committed the offence, having been informed of the alternative measure, fully and freely consents to participate in it`
       AND facts's `(d) the person alleged to have committed the offence has, before consenting to participate in the alternative measure, been advised of the right to be represented by counsel`
       AND facts's `(e) the person alleged to have committed the offence accepts responsibility for the act or omission that forms the basis of the offence`
       AND facts's `(f) in the opinion of the Attorney General or the Attorney General’s agent, there is sufficient evidence to proceed with the prosecution of the offence`
       AND facts's `(g) the prosecution of the offence is not in any way barred at law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Alternative measures may be used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence if the following conditions are met"

-- 715.5 Alternative measures must not be used in respect of a person who (a) denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence; or (b) expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court.
-- A bar. No party is named ("must not be used"), so there is no regulative rule, only the test. JUST TRUE means the bar applies.
-- src:15089 | 715.5 Alternative measures must not be used in respect of a person who
-- src:15090 | (a) denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence; or
-- src:15091 | (b) expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court.
@ref s 715.5 (src:15089-15091)
GIVEN `the person denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.5 alternative measures must not be used in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `the person denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence` OR `the person expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Alternative measures must not be used in respect of a person who (a) denies participation or involvement in the commission of the offence; or (b) expresses the wish to have any charge against them dealt with by the court"

-- 715.51 No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure
-- is admissible in evidence against that person in any civil or criminal proceedings.
-- src:15093 | 715.51 No admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure is admissible in evidence against that person in any civil or criminal proceedings.
@ref s 715.51 (src:15093-15093)
GIVEN `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is offered in evidence against that person in civil or criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.51 the admission is inadmissible in evidence against the person` MEANS
    IF `it is an admission, confession or statement accepting responsibility for a given act or omission` AND `it was made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure` AND `it is offered in evidence against that person in civil or criminal proceedings`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "made by a person alleged to have committed an offence as a condition of the person being dealt with by an alternative measure"

-- 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act,
-- src:15095 | 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act, but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence,
@ref s 715.52(1) (src:15095-15095)
GIVEN `alternative measures have been used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are proceedings against the person under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.52(1) the use of alternative measures is a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act` MEANS
    IF `alternative measures have been used in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence` AND `the proceedings are proceedings against the person under this Act`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act"

-- ... but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence, (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures,
-- the court must dismiss the charge. A duty with an "if" and a "where" ("in the case where"): either failing is JUST FALSE (fork F8).
-- src:15095 | 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act, but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence,
-- src:15096 | (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court must dismiss the charge; and
@ref s 715.52(1)(a) (src:15095-15096)
GIVEN `a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.52(1)(a) the court must dismiss the charge` MEANS
    IF `a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence` AND `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence, (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied"

-- (b) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court may dismiss the charge
-- if, in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and that person's compliance with respect to the alternative measures.
-- A grant ("may") with a "where" gate (listed, JUST FALSE, ruling (b)) and two "if" gates not closed by "only if" (flipped, NOTHING; fork F2).
-- src:15095 | 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act, but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence,
-- src:15096 | (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court must dismiss the charge; and
-- src:15097 | (b) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court may dismiss the charge if, in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and that person’s compliance with respect to the alternative measures.
@ref s 715.52(1)(b) (src:15095-15097)
GIVEN `a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and that person’s compliance with respect to the alternative measures` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.52(1)(b) the court may dismiss the charge` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence"
        IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures` AND `in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and that person’s compliance with respect to the alternative measures` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied ... the court may dismiss the charge if, in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair"

-- 715.52 (2) Subject to subsection (1), nothing in this Part is to be construed as preventing any person from laying an information, obtaining the issue or confirmation of any process or proceeding with the prosecution of any offence, in accordance with the law.
