    `s 715.52(2) laying an information`
    `s 715.52(2) obtaining the issue or confirmation of any process`
    `s 715.52(2) proceeding with the prosecution of any offence`
    `s 715.52(2) an act that none of those names`

@ref s 715.52(2) (src:15099-15099)
GIVEN act IS A `s 715.52(2) the act`
      `the act is done in accordance with the law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1)(a) requires the court to dismiss the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.52(2) this Part is to be construed as preventing the person from doing the act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 715.52(2) an act that none of those names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "from laying an information, obtaining the issue or confirmation of any process or proceeding with the prosecution of any offence"
        IF NOT `the act is done in accordance with the law` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in accordance with the law"
        IF `subsection (1)(a) requires the court to dismiss the charge` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (1)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "nothing in this Part is to be construed as preventing any person from"

§ `Sections 715.53 and 715.54 -- Restorative justice processes`

-- 715.53 The following additional principles apply to the use of restorative justice processes: (a) to (g). A table, as for 715.46.
-- src:15105 | 715.53 The following additional principles apply to the use of restorative justice processes:
-- src:15106 | (a) restorative justice processes prioritize the acknowledgement and acceptance of responsibility for the harm caused to victims and communities and the repair of that harm by the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender;
-- src:15107 | (b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time;
-- src:15108 | (c) they take into consideration the safety and security of all participants and seek to prevent further harm;
-- src:15109 | (d) they are based on courtesy, compassion and respect, including respect for the dignity of all participants;
-- src:15110 | (e) they foster and support the meaningful participation of those affected, including victims, persons alleged to have committed an offence and offenders and their communities;
-- src:15111 | (f) they enable participants to communicate openly and honestly and to have an active role in determining how to address their needs, as they perceive them; and
-- src:15112 | (g) they provide opportunities for understanding, healing and change and contribute to the restoration and recovery of victims and the rehabilitation and reintegration of persons alleged to have committed an offence or offenders.
@ref s 715.53 (src:15105-15112)
DECLARE `s 715.53 the principle` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.53(a) restorative justice processes prioritize the acknowledgement and acceptance of responsibility for the harm caused to victims and communities and the repair of that harm by the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender`
    `s 715.53(b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time`
    `s 715.53(c) they take into consideration the safety and security of all participants and seek to prevent further harm`
    `s 715.53(d) they are based on courtesy, compassion and respect, including respect for the dignity of all participants`
    `s 715.53(e) they foster and support the meaningful participation of those affected, including victims, persons alleged to have committed an offence and offenders and their communities`
    `s 715.53(f) they enable participants to communicate openly and honestly and to have an active role in determining how to address their needs, as they perceive them`
    `s 715.53(g) they provide opportunities for understanding, healing and change and contribute to the restoration and recovery of victims and the rehabilitation and reintegration of persons alleged to have committed an offence or offenders`
    `s 715.53 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (g) names`

@ref s 715.53 (src:15105-15112)
GIVEN principle IS A `s 715.53 the principle`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.53 the principle applies to the use of restorative justice processes` MEANS
    CONSIDER principle
    WHEN `s 715.53(a) restorative justice processes prioritize the acknowledgement and acceptance of responsibility for the harm caused to victims and communities and the repair of that harm by the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(c) they take into consideration the safety and security of all participants and seek to prevent further harm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(d) they are based on courtesy, compassion and respect, including respect for the dignity of all participants` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(e) they foster and support the meaningful participation of those affected, including victims, persons alleged to have committed an offence and offenders and their communities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(f) they enable participants to communicate openly and honestly and to have an active role in determining how to address their needs, as they perceive them` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53(g) they provide opportunities for understanding, healing and change and contribute to the restoration and recovery of victims and the rehabilitation and reintegration of persons alleged to have committed an offence or offenders` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.53 a statement that none of paragraphs (a) to (g) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The following additional principles apply to the use of restorative justice processes"

-- 715.53 (b), read as a function of one participant: participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw at any time.
-- The principle names the participants; for a person who is not one the text does not answer.
-- src:15107 | (b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time;
@ref s 715.53(b) (src:15107-15107)
GIVEN `the person is a participant in the restorative justice process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.53(b) the participant must fully and freely consent to participate` MEANS
    IF `the person is a participant in the restorative justice process`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "participants must fully and freely consent to participate"

-- src:15107 | (b) they are voluntary and participants must fully and freely consent to participate and may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time;
@ref s 715.53(b) (src:15107-15107)
GIVEN `the person is a participant in the restorative justice process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.53(b) the participant may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time` MEANS
    IF `the person is a participant in the restorative justice process`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "participants ... may freely withdraw from the restorative justice process at any time"

-- 715.54 (1) A restorative justice process may be used at any stage of a criminal justice process, including as an alternative measure.
-- src:15114 | 715.54 (1) A restorative justice process may be used at any stage of a criminal justice process, including as an alternative measure.
@ref s 715.54(1) (src:15114-15114)
GIVEN `it is a stage of a criminal justice process` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.54(1) a restorative justice process may be used at the stage` MEANS
    IF `it is a stage of a criminal justice process`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any stage of a criminal justice process"

-- 715.54 (2) A restorative justice process may take various forms, including in the form of a mediation or dialogue between the victim and the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender, a restorative conference or a sentencing circle.
-- src:15116 | (2) A restorative justice process may take various forms, including in the form of a mediation or dialogue between the victim and the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender, a restorative conference or a sentencing circle.
@ref s 715.54(2) (src:15116-15116)
DECLARE `s 715.54(2) the form` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.54(2) a mediation or dialogue between the victim and the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender`
    `s 715.54(2) a restorative conference`
    `s 715.54(2) a sentencing circle`
    `s 715.54(2) a form that none of those names`

@ref s 715.54(2) (src:15116-15116)
GIVEN form IS A `s 715.54(2) the form`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.54(2) a restorative justice process may take the form` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `s 715.54(2) a mediation or dialogue between the victim and the person alleged to have committed an offence or the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.54(2) a restorative conference` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.54(2) a sentencing circle` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.54(2) a form that none of those names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may take various forms, including"

-- 715.54 (3) For greater certainty, sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply when a restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part.
-- The sections are named by number, so the test takes the core's `Provision of the Code` (seam rule R1). Section numbers are decimals: 715.5 is section 715.5 and sits between 715.49 and 715.51 (715.5 = 715.50).
-- "When" gate: failing it is JUST FALSE by the ruling of 2026-11-04/05 (fork F13: the clause is introduced "For greater certainty", and a reader may take it as declaratory only, which would make the answer NOTHING).
-- src:15118 | (3) For greater certainty, sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply when a restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part.
@ref s 715.54(3) (src:15118-15118)
GIVEN provision IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.54(3) the provision applies to the restorative justice process` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (provision's `section` AT LEAST 715.49 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 715.52) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sections 715.49 to 715.52 apply"
        IF `the restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when a restorative justice process is used as an alternative measure under this Part"

§ `Section 715.55 -- Conferences`

-- 715.55 (1) A judge, justice or any person authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3) may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference,
-- in which a prosecutor, a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender, and any other person who could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2), participate.
-- A grant ("may") with no "if": the text names who may convene. The core has no constructor for a person authorized under the rules, so that person is an input flag (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- src:15122 | 715.55 (1) A judge, justice or any person authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3) may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference, in which a prosecutor, a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender, and any other person who could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2), participate.
@ref s 715.55(1) (src:15122-15122)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `the person is authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.55(1) the person may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference` MEANS
    IF (person EQUALS `a judge`) OR (person EQUALS `a justice`) OR `the person is authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judge, justice or any person authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3) may"

@ref s 715.55(1) (src:15122-15122)
GIVEN person IS A Party
      `the person could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.55(1) the person participates in the conference` MEANS
    IF (person EQUALS `the prosecutor`) OR (person EQUALS `the accused`) OR (person EQUALS `the offender`) OR `the person could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which a prosecutor, a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender, and any other person who could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2), participate"

-- 715.55 (2) The objective of a conference is, among other things, to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence or the offender
-- and to make recommendations, if appropriate, in respect of resolution options, treatment plans, counselling and health and social services.
-- src:15124 | (2) The objective of a conference is, among other things, to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence or the offender and to make recommendations, if appropriate, in respect of resolution options, treatment plans, counselling and health and social services.
@ref s 715.55(2) (src:15124-15124)
DECLARE `s 715.55(2) the objective` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.55(2) to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence or the offender`
    `s 715.55(2) to make recommendations, if appropriate, in respect of resolution options, treatment plans, counselling and health and social services`
    `s 715.55(2) an objective that neither of those names`

@ref s 715.55(2) (src:15124-15124)
GIVEN objective IS A `s 715.55(2) the objective`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.55(2) the objective is an objective of a conference` MEANS
    CONSIDER objective
    WHEN `s 715.55(2) to facilitate the use of alternative measures or restorative justice processes in respect of the person alleged to have committed the offence or the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.55(2) to make recommendations, if appropriate, in respect of resolution options, treatment plans, counselling and health and social services` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 715.55(2) an objective that neither of those names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The objective of a conference is, among other things"

-- 715.55 (3) The Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of conferences,
-- other than for conferences convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice. The exclusion is in the text's own words (kept JUST FALSE). "Other than" is not among the closing words the name-test sweep lists ("only if", "only where", "may not ... unless", a list closed with "only"), so keeping JUST FALSE here is my judgment, one of the "(other than X)" sites decided case by case (fork F28; the other reading is NOTHING, a grant limited in its own wording).
-- src:15126 | (3) The Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of conferences, other than for conferences convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice.
@ref s 715.55(3) (src:15126-15126)
GIVEN `the person is the Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conference is convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.55(3) the person may establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of the conference` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the conference is convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than for conferences convened or caused to be convened by a judge or justice"
        IF `the person is the Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Attorney General or any other minister designated by the lieutenant governor in council of a province may establish"

-- 715.55 (4) In provinces and territories where rules and practices are established under subsection (3), the conferences to which those rules and practices apply must be convened and conducted in accordance with those rules and practices.
-- No party is named ("must be convened and conducted"), so there is no regulative rule. A "where" gate on a duty: failing it is JUST FALSE.
-- src:15128 | (4) In provinces and territories where rules and practices are established under subsection (3), the conferences to which those rules and practices apply must be convened and conducted in accordance with those rules and practices.
@ref s 715.55(4) (src:15128-15128)
GIVEN `rules and practices are established under subsection (3) in the province or territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those rules and practices apply to the conference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.55(4) the conference must be convened and conducted in accordance with the rules and practices` MEANS
    IF `rules and practices are established under subsection (3) in the province or territory` AND `those rules and practices apply to the conference`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In provinces and territories where rules and practices are established under subsection (3), the conferences to which those rules and practices apply"

§ `Sections 715.56 to 715.6 -- Records`

-- 715.56 Sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48, regardless of the degree of their compliance with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures.
-- "Apply only" closes the gate: for a provision in the range and a person who has not been issued a warning or referral the answer is JUST FALSE. Decimals: 715.6 is section 715.6 = 715.60, after 715.59.
-- src:15132 | 715.56 Sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48, regardless of the degree of their compliance with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures.
