      `the person has been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.56 the provision applies in respect of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (provision's `section` AT LEAST 715.57 AND provision's `section` AT MOST 715.6) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Sections 715.57 to 715.6 apply"
        IF `the person has been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "apply only in respect of persons who have been issued a warning or a referral under section 715.47 or 715.48"

