    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "information obtained by the person or organization as a result of the use of alternative measures"

-- 715.6 (1) Any information contained in a record that is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59 may be made available to (a) any judge or court for any purpose relating to proceedings relating to offences committed or alleged to have been committed by the person to whom the record relates;
-- (b) any peace officer (i) for the purpose of investigating any offence that the person is suspected on reasonable grounds of having committed, or in respect of which the person has been arrested or charged, or (ii) for any purpose related to the administration of the case to which the record relates;
-- (c) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is (i) engaged in the administration of alternative measures in respect of the person, or (ii) preparing a report in respect of the person as required under this Act; or
-- (d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record, to the extent directed by the judge, if the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is (i) desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes, or (ii) desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
-- A grant ("may be made available"). Paragraph (d) has an "if" gate that the text does not close with "only if": unmet, the answer is NOTHING (fork F2), and "to the extent directed by the judge" limits the grant (fork F14: the extent is the judge's, an input).
-- src:15149 | 715.6 (1) Any information contained in a record that is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59 may be made available to
-- src:15150 | (a) any judge or court for any purpose relating to proceedings relating to offences committed or alleged to have been committed by the person to whom the record relates;
-- src:15151 | (b) any peace officer
-- src:15152 | (i) for the purpose of investigating any offence that the person is suspected on reasonable grounds of having committed, or in respect of which the person has been arrested or charged, or
-- src:15153 | (ii) for any purpose related to the administration of the case to which the record relates;
-- src:15154 | (c) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is
-- src:15155 | (i) engaged in the administration of alternative measures in respect of the person, or
-- src:15156 | (ii) preparing a report in respect of the person as required under this Act; or
-- src:15157 | (d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record, to the extent directed by the judge, if the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is
-- src:15158 | (i) desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes, or
-- src:15159 | (ii) desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 715.6(1) (src:15149-15159)
DECLARE `s 715.6(1) the recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.6(1)(a) any judge or court, for any purpose relating to proceedings relating to offences committed or alleged to have been committed by the person to whom the record relates`
    `s 715.6(1)(b)(i) any peace officer, for the purpose of investigating any offence that the person is suspected on reasonable grounds of having committed, or in respect of which the person has been arrested or charged`
    `s 715.6(1)(b)(ii) any peace officer, for any purpose related to the administration of the case to which the record relates`
    `s 715.6(1)(c)(i) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is engaged in the administration of alternative measures in respect of the person`
    `s 715.6(1)(c)(ii) any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is preparing a report in respect of the person as required under this Act`
    `s 715.6(1)(d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record`
    `s 715.6(1) a recipient that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names`

@ref s 715.6(1) (src:15149-15159)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 715.6(1) the recipient`
      `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(1) the information may be made available to the recipient` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any information contained in a record that is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59"
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 715.6(1) a recipient that none of paragraphs (a) to (d) names` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made available to (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d)"
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 715.6(1)(d) any other person who is deemed, or any person within a class of persons that is deemed, by a judge of a court to have a valid interest in the record` THEN
            IF `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes` OR `the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the judge is satisfied that the disclosure is (i) desirable in the public interest for research or statistical purposes, or (ii) desirable in the interest of the proper administration of justice"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 715.6 (2) Information contained in the record, other than the identity of the person to whom the record relates, may be made available to any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency,
-- that is engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures and assessing their effectiveness, including for research or statistical purposes.
-- "Other than the identity" limits the grant and the text says nothing about the identity itself, so for the identity the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (fork F15).
-- src:15161 | (2) Information contained in the record, other than the identity of the person to whom the record relates, may be made available to any member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or any agent of the department or agency, that is engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures and assessing their effectiveness, including for research or statistical purposes.
@ref s 715.6(2) (src:15161-15161)
GIVEN `the information is information other than the identity of the person to whom the record relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recipient is a member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or an agent of the department or agency, engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures and assessing their effectiveness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(2) the information may be made available to the recipient` MEANS
    IF `the information is information other than the identity of the person to whom the record relates` AND `the recipient is a member of a department or agency of a government in Canada, or an agent of the department or agency, engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures and assessing their effectiveness`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Information contained in the record, other than the identity of the person to whom the record relates, may be made available to any member of a department or agency ... that is engaged in assessing and monitoring the use of alternative measures"

-- 715.6 (3) If a record is made available for inspection to any person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i), that person may subsequently disclose information contained in the record but may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates.
-- Two functions. The grant to disclose has an "if" gate (flipped, NOTHING; fork F2.7) and a "may not" that closes it for the identifying form (kept JUST FALSE).
-- The bar is a flat "may not" in the grant's own sentence. It speaks only of a person to whom a record was made available under (1)(d)(i), and of an identifying form, so outside either the answer is NOTHING (fork F30; the other reading is JUST FALSE for a person to whom no record was made available, a failed "If" on a bar).
-- src:15163 | (3) If a record is made available for inspection to any person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i), that person may subsequently disclose information contained in the record but may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates.
@ref s 715.6(3) (src:15163-15163)
GIVEN `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(3) the person may subsequently disclose the information contained in the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a record is made available for inspection to any person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i), that person may subsequently disclose"
        IF `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 715.6(3) (src:15163-15163)
GIVEN `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(3) the person may not disclose the information in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates` MEANS
    IF `the record is made available for inspection to the person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i)` AND `the information is disclosed in a form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a record is made available for inspection to any person under subparagraph (1)(d)(i), ... may not disclose the information in any form that would reasonably be expected to identify the person to whom it relates"

-- 715.6 (4) Any person to whom a record is authorized to be made available under this section may be given any information contained in the record and may be given a copy of any part of the record.
-- src:15165 | (4) Any person to whom a record is authorized to be made available under this section may be given any information contained in the record and may be given a copy of any part of the record.
@ref s 715.6(4) (src:15165-15165)
GIVEN `a record is authorized to be made available to the person under section 715.6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(4) the person may be given the information contained in the record and a copy of any part of the record` MEANS
    IF `a record is authorized to be made available to the person under section 715.6`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person to whom a record is authorized to be made available under this section"

-- 715.6 (5) Evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral, evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence and evidence of the offence are inadmissible
-- for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour in any proceedings before a court in respect of the individual.
-- src:15167 | (5) Evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral, evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence and evidence of the offence are inadmissible for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour in any proceedings before a court in respect of the individual.
@ref s 715.6(5) (src:15167-15167)
DECLARE `s 715.6(5) the evidence` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.6(5) evidence that an individual has received a warning or referral`
    `s 715.6(5) evidence that a police officer has taken no further action in respect of an offence`
    `s 715.6(5) evidence of the offence`
    `s 715.6(5) evidence that none of those names`

@ref s 715.6(5) (src:15167-15167)
GIVEN evidence IS A `s 715.6(5) the evidence`
      `it is offered for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is offered in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(5) the evidence is inadmissible` MEANS
    IF (NOT (evidence EQUALS `s 715.6(5) evidence that none of those names`)) AND `it is offered for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour` AND `it is offered in proceedings before a court in respect of the individual`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "inadmissible for the purpose of proving prior offending behaviour in any proceedings before a court in respect of the individual"

-- 715.6 (6) A record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59 may not be introduced into evidence, except for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c), more than two years after the end of the period during which the alternative measure was applied.
-- A bar: JUST TRUE means the bar applies. The two-year point is the second anniversary of the end of the period (`add years` clamps 29 February to 28 February: fork F11). "More than" is after that day, so on the day itself the bar does not yet apply.
-- src:15169 | (6) A record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59 may not be introduced into evidence, except for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c), more than two years after the end of the period during which the alternative measure was applied.
@ref s 715.6(6) (src:15169-15169)
GIVEN `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the introduction into evidence is for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the record is introduced into evidence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the period during which the alternative measure was applied ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 715.6(6) the record may not be introduced into evidence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the record is kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A record kept under any of sections 715.57 to 715.59"
        IF `the introduction into evidence is for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except for the purposes set out in paragraph 721(3)(c)"
        IF `the day on which the record is introduced into evidence` AT MOST `the second anniversary of the end of the period` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "more than two years after the end of the period during which the alternative measure was applied"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `the second anniversary of the end of the period` MEANS `add years` `the day on which the period during which the alternative measure was applied ended` 2

§ `Regulative rules of sections 715.47 to 715.58 (the same duties and permissions, run with #TRACE in the tests file)`

-- Each rule below is the duty, permission or bar ONCE IT HAS ARISEN, and carries no gate. The conditions under which it arises ("if", "where", "when", "after") are tested by the decision function of the same section, and the #TRACE runs in the tests file show what follows from doing or not doing the act, never whether the duty arose.

-- Parties are the core's Party type. No deadline, consequence or remedy is added that the text does not state: where the text gives no time limit the rule has no WITHIN,
-- so a duty not yet performed shows as a standing obligation and never as a breach.
DECLARE `s 715.47 to 715.58 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 715.47(1) consider taking no further action, issuing a warning, or referring the person`
    `s 715.48(1) consider issuing a warning or referring the person`
    `s 715.52(1)(a) dismiss the charge`
    `s 715.52(1)(b) dismiss the charge on partial compliance`
    `s 715.55(1) convene or cause to be convened a conference`
    `s 715.55(3) establish rules and practices for the convening and conducting of conferences`
    `s 715.57 keep a record of the warning issued or referral made`
    `s 715.58(2) disclose information in a record to any person`
    `s 715.58(3) disclose information in a record to an insurance company`

-- src:15061 | 715.47 (1) A police officer must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, instead of proceeding with the laying of an information against the person alleged to have committed the offence,
@ref s 715.47(1) (src:15061-15061)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.47 to 715.58 act`
`s 715.47(1) the police officer's duty to consider the options` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `s 715.47(1) consider taking no further action, issuing a warning, or referring the person`

-- src:15068 | 715.48 (1) A prosecutor must, if it is appropriate in the circumstances and does not pose a risk to the safety of the public, while taking into account the interests of the victim, of society and of the person alleged to have committed an offence and having regard to the purpose and principles set out in sections 715.45 and 715.46, consider, before commencing or continuing judicial proceedings against the person alleged to have committed the offence,
@ref s 715.48(1) (src:15068-15068)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.47 to 715.58 act`
`s 715.48(1) the prosecutor's duty to consider the options` MEANS
    PARTY `the prosecutor`
    MUST `s 715.48(1) consider issuing a warning or referring the person`

-- src:15095 | 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act, but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence,
-- src:15096 | (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court must dismiss the charge; and
@ref s 715.52(1)(a) (src:15095-15096)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.47 to 715.58 act`
`s 715.52(1)(a) the court's duty to dismiss the charge` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 715.52(1)(a) dismiss the charge`

-- src:15095 | 715.52 (1) The use of alternative measures in respect of a person alleged to have committed an offence is not a bar to proceedings against the person under this Act, but, in the case where a charge is laid against that person in respect of that offence,
-- src:15096 | (a) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has totally complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court must dismiss the charge; and
-- src:15097 | (b) if the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the person has partially complied with the terms and conditions of the alternative measures, the court may dismiss the charge if, in the opinion of the court, the prosecution of the charge would be unfair, having regard to the circumstances and that person’s compliance with respect to the alternative measures.
@ref s 715.52(1)(b) (src:15095-15097)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 715.47 to 715.58 act`
`s 715.52(1)(b) the court's permission to dismiss the charge` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MAY `s 715.52(1)(b) dismiss the charge on partial compliance`

-- src:15122 | 715.55 (1) A judge, justice or any person authorized under the rules and practices referred to in subsection (3) may, on request or on their own initiative, convene or cause to be convened a conference, in which a prosecutor, a person alleged to have committed an offence or an offender, and any other person who could assist with the objectives set out in subsection (2), participate.
